delight:
Yea, Thou dost stop with me this vigil night;
To-night of pain, to-morrow of delight:
I, Love, am Thine; Thou, Lord my God, art mine.

deluded:
And laid it on a chair;
And men by drink deluded
Knelt by that badge in prayer.

delirium:
I recollect as, after fevers, men
Thread back the passage of delirium,
Missing the turn still, baffled by the door;

delaware:
Dim are the volumes of eld;
Else had old Delaware told us
More that her history held.

dell:
I labor hard, and toil and sweat,
While others dream within the dell;
But even while my brow is wet,

dely:
Delikit an' slendah.
Dely brown ez brown kin be
An' huh haih is curly;
